  "solution": "**Calculation:**\n\nLet the sum be P and the rate of interest be r\n\nSimple interest = PRT/100\n\n⇒ 1050 = P + PR × (5/100)\n\n⇒ P(1 + 5R/100) = 1050 -------(1)\n\n⇒ 1230 = P + PR × (8/100)\n\n⇒ P(1 + 8R/100) = 1230 -------(2)\n\nSolving (1) and (2), \n\n⇒ (1 + 5R/100)/(1 + 8R/100) = 1050/1230\n\n⇒ (1 + 5R/100)/(1 + 8R/100) = 35/41\n\n⇒ 41(1 + 5R/100) = 35(1 + 8R/100)\n\n⇒ 41 + 205R/100 = 35 + 280R/100\n\n⇒ 75R/100 = 6\n\n⇒ R = 6 × 4/3\n\n⇒ R = 8%\n\nPut the value in (1)\n\n⇒ P(1 + 5 × 8/100) = 1050 \n\n⇒ P = 1050 × 5/7\n\n⇒ P = Rs. 750\n\n**∴ Option 4 is the correct answer.**",
